    s__DIG_OVER_METHOD(py_str("One spade deep is enough for most beds: turn the soil over, break up the clods and fork a couple of buckets of compost or well-rotted manure into each square metre as you go. Pick out every white root of bindweed and nettle as it comes up, or it will be back within weeks. Autumn is the best time, because the frost breaks the clods down for you, and leave it alone if the soil is wet enough to ball in your hand - digging clay when it is wet turns it into brick."));
    s__DIG_OVER_WHEN(py_str("Autumn, from October into December, once the beds are emptying: dig it over then and the frost does the work of breaking the clods down over winter, so the soil is workable in spring. On heavy clay that is the one time it is worth doing, because digging wet clay turns it into brick and digging dry clay leaves the lumps like stones. If you have to do it in spring, fork it over rather than digging."));
